    "question": {
      ":question/id": "24ae883a-52d9-54d8-9649-4854830a677c",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(A)=-1$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$\n\nIII. $A\\text{ does not have }6\\text{ pivot columns}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=6 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=-1$, so $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=6$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{6}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $A\\text{ is invertible}$. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true: $\\text{rank}(A)=6$. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\n- Statement III is false: $A\\text{ does not have }6\\text{ pivot columns}$. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and II only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
